wikipedia_extract: The Japanese aircraft carrier Unryū (雲龍, Cloud Dragon) was the
  lead ship of her class of fleet aircraft carriers built for the Imperial Japanese
  Navy (IJN) during World War II. She was commissioned in mid-1944, but fuel and aircrew
  shortages limited her use to Japanese waters. The impending American invasion of
  Luzon caused the IJN to order her to transport aircraft and supplies to the Philippines
  in December. The ship was torpedoed and sunk by the American submarine USS Redfish
  in the East China Sea during the voyage.
